# Source of truth for CI and local development. Compile to requirements.txt WITH HASHES:
#   uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.11 --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#   (or: pip install pip-tools && pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt)
# Commit both files. The lock file is what makes the build reproducible, and CI installs
# it with --require-hashes so an unpinned or tampered package fails the build.
#
# The Azure ML SDK is NOT here. Lab 2's remote-training tools need it, but azureml-core
# pins a ruamel.yaml that cannot build on Python 3.11, which made this lock uninstallable
# in CI. It lives in requirements-azure.in for `make setup-azure`.
